  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate-Resilient Flood Protection Dams Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims at achieving a high level of flood risk control in four critical areas in the Sultanate of Oman: WADI MAJLASS Dam in Quriyat Province, Muscat Governorate; WADI AL-KHAWD Dam in Al Seeb Province,  Muscat Governate; WADI AHIN Dam in Saham Province, North Al Batinah Governorate; and WADI RIJMA Dam in Shinas Province, North Al Batinah Governorate. By enhancing flood protection infrastructure, the project will secure these urban and developing areas against the recurring threat of floods. Additionally, the project will contribute to the improvement of groundwater recharge downstream.</narrative>
  </description>
